WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.470
Three plans.

2
00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.380
Twenty-three strategies.

3
00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:05.210
In the last two videos you learned

4
00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.430
to read a card and the Catalog.

5
00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.760
This time we go plan by plan and

6
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.550
look at what is actually inside each one.

7
00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:15.590
Every figure you will see is a simulated backtest,

8
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:19.230
not real performance, and not investment advice.

9
00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.260
Entry is one strategy:

10
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.760
Bitcoin, one decision a day.

11
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.140
It is our flagship and the

12
00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.870
card you have already seen.

13
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:28.640
Today it is in cash.

14
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.870
It sold Bitcoin on October thirteenth,

15
00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:34.070
closing that trade at plus seventeen point eight percent,

16
00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.590
and it has waited since.

17
00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.540
If you want to learn how

18
00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.760
a signal behaves before anything else,

19
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.760
this is the card.

20
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.310
Intermediate adds fourteen strategies,

21
00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.590
and all of them are long only.

22
00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:48.040
They hold an asset or they hold cash.

23
00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.960
No shorts, no perpetuals,

24
00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.510
no leverage: a plain spot account is enough.

25
00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:56.050
Three things appear here for the first time.

26
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:59.280
More assets, including gold and two stocks.

27
00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.930
A faster clock: twelve hours.

28
00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:06.280
And rotations, one rule that moves across several assets.

29
00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.360
We call a single-asset strategy a sovereign.

30
00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.270
Intermediate has them on Ethereum,

31
00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.870
Solana and SUI, daily.

32
00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:16.080
Here is ETH 1D.

33
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.640
It is in cash too:

34
00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.830
it sold Ethereum on October eighth,

35
00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.950
and that trade closed at plus forty-four percent.

36
00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.710
Same card layout as Bitcoin,

37
00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.390
same rules for reading it.

38
00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.030
Gold joins the line-up with PAXG,

39
00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:31.110
daily and twelve-hour.

40
00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:32.920
Gold is the calm one.

41
00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.230
Its numbers are the smallest in the catalog,

42
00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:36.590
and so is the drop:

43
00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:39.480
about fifteen percent at worst in the backtest.

44
00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.180
It is also one of the five assets a

45
00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:44.390
rotation can park in when crypto is weak.

46
00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:46.830
Some cards say two decisions a day.

47
00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.840
A twelve-hour strategy looks at the market

48
00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.480
at midnight and at noon UTC,

49
00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:52.760
so it reacts faster,

50
00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.600
in both directions.

51
00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.080
We adapted the Bitcoin rule to that clock,

52
00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.730
and on the common window it earned its place:

53
00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:03.040
BTC 12H, seventy percent a year

54
00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.900
against fifty-four for the daily card,

55
00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:06.180
with the same drawdown,

56
00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.070
about seventeen percent.

57
00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:09.480
Let us go back a week.

58
00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.610
On October twenty-third this card was long Bitcoin.

59
00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.340
Today it is in cash:

60
00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.970
it exited on the twenty-fourth at plus twenty-six percent.

61
00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.310
Open the full card.

62
00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:22.620
Strategy against holding, same one thousand dollars,

63
00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.480
same start.

64
00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.590
And the price chart:

65
00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:26.310
orange while it held Bitcoin,

66
00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:28.200
green while it sat in cash,

67
00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.830
on the window you choose.

68
00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.730
Faster is not free.

69
00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:34.800
More decisions mean more trades and more commissions,

70
00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.680
so every twelve-hour card has to earn

71
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:38.990
its place against its daily sibling,

72
00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:40.280
and the Summary lets you

73
00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:42.000
compare them side by side.

74
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.960
A rotation is one rule applied

75
00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.020
to several assets at once:

76
00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.970
Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana, SUI and gold.

77
00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:52.230
Each day it holds the strongest of them,

78
00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.440
or cash.

79
00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.680
Intermediate has five: Rotation 1D,

80
00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:00.590
Rotation 12H, Rotation 1D Proportional,

81
00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:02.480
Rotation 1D with stocks,

82
00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:05.030
and Portfolio 1D Stocks.

83
00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.200
Open the Summary and set

84
00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.030
the window to one year.

85
00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:09.740
Filter by rotation.

86
00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:12.350
Rotation 12H is the best long-only

87
00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:14.430
product of the last twelve months:

88
00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.010
one hundred four percent a year,

89
00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:19.550
eighteen percent drawdown, two decisions a day.

90
00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.270
Now the Proportional one.

91
00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.450
Instead of one asset,

92
00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:24.760
it splits the capital by strength.

93
00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.190
On October seventh its card held three:

94
00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:30.500
Solana forty-two percent, SUI thirty-three,

95
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.070
Ethereum twenty-four.

96
00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:34.050
The next day, only SUI.

97
00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.330
Since the eighteenth, cash.

98
00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.590
Scroll down the card:

99
00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:40.260
a rotation reports cash to cash,

100
00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:41.580
the result of the whole stay in

101
00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.630
the market across every asset it held.

102
00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.520
Two stocks are in Intermediate:

103
00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.740
MicroStrategy and Tesla.

104
00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:50.030
We chose them because they are

105
00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:52.390
volatile enough to behave like crypto,

106
00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:54.270
and the same rule works on them.

107
00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:55.940
You get them as sovereigns,

108
00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:59.190
MSTR 1D and TSLA 1D,

109
00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:01.710
inside Rotation 1D with stocks,

110
00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.850
and in Portfolio 1D Stocks,

111
00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.670
which rotates between the two stocks and gold.

112
00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:09.790
Stock cards decide after the New York close.

113
00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.810
Today TSLA 1D is long,

114
00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.930
since October twenty-second, and Portfolio 1D Stocks

115
00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:18.270
is one hundred percent in Tesla.

116
00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:21.420
Expert adds eight long and short strategies.

117
00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.690
A short is a bet on a fall:

118
00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:25.360
you sell an asset you do not

119
00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.340
own and buy it back lower.

120
00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:28.510
To do that you need a

121
00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:31.430
margin or perpetual account and collateral.

122
00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:32.790
Your loss is not capped the

123
00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.290
way it is when you hold,

124
00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.450
and the exchange can close you out.

125
00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.450
It is harder and riskier,

126
00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:41.030
which is why this tier is called Expert.

127
00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:44.150
Here is MSTR 1D L+S today:

128
00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.740
one hundred percent MicroStrategy,

129
00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:49.080
short, since October twenty-eighth.

130
00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:53.940
Shorts lose too: Rotation 12H L+S shorted SUI

131
00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:56.540
on the twenty-sixth and closed it two days

132
00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.970
later at minus three point seven percent.

133
00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:01.190
Now the Summary on the common window.

134
00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:04.780
Row one is Rotation 1D LS with stocks.

135
00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.440
In this simulated backtest,

136
00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:09.740
since May 2023, one thousand twenty-five percent

137
00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:12.630
a year with a twenty-two percent drawdown.

138
00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.720
Its long-only twin, row two,

139
00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.750
did six hundred forty-one.

140
00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:20.890
Both are extraordinary numbers from one in-sample backtest.

141
00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:22.920
Long and short strategies are in early

142
00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.230
access and their results are preliminary.

143
00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:26.900
Read them as a rule's history,

144
00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:28.910
not as a promise.

145
00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:30.700
Entry for a first look.

146
00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:33.470
Intermediate for the whole long-only line.

147
00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:35.630
Expert if you also want shorts,

148
00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:37.380
knowing what they ask of you.

149
00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.670
Everything here is a simulated backtest,

150
00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:42.970
not real performance, and not investment advice.

